       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f734cd2bc550ef0625a7d6c498d9ee12?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGR-4.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f734cd2bc550ef0625a7d6c498d9ee12?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGR-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f734cd2bc550ef0625a7d6c498d9ee12?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGR-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f734cd2bc550ef0625a7d6c498d9ee12?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGR-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Glen Robson",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A2487a0d3-3c28-4d3a-8be4-d4908219518a",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I setup two Fedora instances with legacyfs and Journaling to keep them in sync. When I ingested an object with a managed datastream the layout on the file system is as follows:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Directory layout:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "/usr/local/fedora/data/datastreams/2014/1018/20/48 - primary",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "/usr/local/fedora/data/datastreams/2014/1018/20/53 - secondary",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Object dir:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "/usr/local/fedora/data/objects/2014/1003/23/34/llgc-id_1 - primary",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "/usr/local/fedora/data/objects/2014/1003/23/39/llgc-id_1 - secondary",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "i.e. the directory and file layout is different between the primary and secondary. Does this break the Repository Equivalence rule:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA37/Journaling#Journaling-intro-equiv"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA37/Journaling#Journaling-intro-equiv",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "It may not be a big issue but if you are only backing up the secondary (this may be the case if you can't do a hot backup on the primary) then you can't restore the primary database as the paths would be different on the secondary. I can't think of many other situations where this would be a problem. ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
